.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux \- A unified suite of PowerToys\-style micro\-utilities for Linux
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
PowerToys\-style micro\-utilities for Linux, in one binary.
.PP
Run without a subcommand to open the GTK control center. Each subcommand runs one utility from the terminal, a script or a keyboard shortcut.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
powerlinux\-ocr(1)
Select a screen region and copy the recognized text to the clipboard
.TP
powerlinux\-pick\-color(1)
Pick a color from the screen and copy its HEX value
.TP
powerlinux\-color(1)
Convert a color (#hex or rgb(...)) and report WCAG contrast
.TP
powerlinux\-compress(1)
Strip metadata and compress PNG, JPEG, WebP or MP4 files
.TP
powerlinux\-expand(1)
Expand a snippet template, e.g. "Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}"
.TP
powerlinux\-picker(1)
Open the snippet picker and paste the chosen snippet into the focused app
.TP
powerlinux\-expander(1)
Set up and toggle typed triggers (type ;date anywhere to expand it)
.TP
powerlinux\-daemon(1)
Run the background service that listens for global shortcuts
.TP
powerlinux\-doctor(1)
Check that everything PowerLinux needs is installed and set up
.TP
powerlinux\-trigger(1)
Run a hotkey action via the daemon, or directly if it isn\*(Aqt running
.TP
powerlinux\-shortcuts(1)
Manage GNOME keybindings for desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the control center:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Copy text from part of the screen:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux ocr\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check a color\*(Aqs contrast:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux color \*(Aq#3584e4\*(Aq\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start the background service at every login:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux daemon enable\-autostart\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/powerlinux/config.toml\fR
Configuration: hotkeys, OCR language, compression quality and snippets. Every key is optional.
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/powerlinux/colors.txt\fR
Color history, newest first, shared by pick\-color, the daemon and the control center.
.TP
\fB~/.config/autostart/io.github.powerlinux.Daemon.desktop\fR
Created by powerlinux daemon enable\-autostart.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR
When set, the clipboard is accessed with wl\-copy and wl\-paste; otherwise with xclip.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
Override the base directories of the files listed above.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
0 on success, 1 on any error. Errors are printed to standard error.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\-ocr\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-pick\-color\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-color\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-compress\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-expand\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-picker\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-expander\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-daemon\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-doctor\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-trigger\fR(1), \fBpowerlinux\-shortcuts\fR(1)
